## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CKNE implementation in multi-tenant data-export scenarios, requiring clear resource mapping, dynamic reallocation logic, and SLA preservation.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-resource allocation mapping
- Minute-granularity reallocation cycles
- Baseline SLA guarantees with fair preemption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simplified allocation function
function allocateExportSlots(tenants, maxSlots) {
  const baseline = 1;
  const allocated = tenants.map(t => ({
    ...t,
    slots: Math.max(baseline, Math.round(t.ckne * maxSlots))
  }));
  return rebalanceToMaxSlots(allocated, maxSlots);
}
```

## Test Plan
1. Verify baseline allocation: tenants with ckne=0.1 receive 1 slot
2. Test proportional scaling: ckne=0.5 receives 4 slots with MAX_SLOTS=8
3. Validate reallocation: low-CKNE tenants deprioritized when high-CKNE tenants join
4. Confirm SLA preservation: minimum 1 slot maintained during all scenarios

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-hop, CKNE-aware backpressure and fairness across thousands of tenants with SLA-based tuning.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health as a control signal for fan-out
- Per-tenant token bucket and dynamic scaling
- SLA-tier influences on limits and queuing
- Edge backpressure signaling and aggregation
- Payload schemas and end-to-end test plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeLimit(health, queueLen, sla) {
  const base = 1000;
  if (health > 0.8 && queueLen < sla.maxQueue * 0.7) return Math.min(base * 5, sla.maxCap);
  if (health < 0.4 || queueLen > sla.maxQueue * 0.9) return Math.max(base * 0.2, sla.minCap);
  return base;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design CKNE-aware real-time scheduling for multi-tenant streaming, focusing on dynamic backpressure, fairness, and latency SLAs.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-based rate shaping and budgets
- Token bucket backpressure per tenant
- Dynamic shard/windowing allocation
- Latency SLA preservation and telemetry

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal token bucket sketch
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  consume(n=1){
    const now = Date.now();
    const delta = (now - this.last) * this.rate / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + delta);
    this.last = now;
    if(this.tokens >= n){ this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

